File Handling - Images, PDF's, Excels, etc. are all Files only. to read and write back these Files with Java code.
    Two ways in which Files are handled :
        1. Byte Streams
            a. File Input Streams -> read a file
            b. File Output Streams -> write into a file
        2. Character Streams
            a. File Reader -> read a file
            b. File Writer -> write into a file

        /* we generally access data in form stream/ write back in form stream. Like this java reads and writes data from files. for this it uses two ways-
            - Character streams : reads in Character mode (unicode) (reads two bytes as Character size is 2 bytes) ('A') Character streams support all characters
            - Byte streams : Byte stream reads data in form of bytes. (single byte of data is read from file) ('A' - 65) Byte streams do not support all characters
        */


